    owner: "Ame-no-Wakahiko",
    maker: "Unknown (bestowed by the gods of heaven)",
    power: "A feathered arrow given with the heavenly bow; shot upward, it flew all the way to heaven and came back.",
    firstRecord: "Kojiki",
    summary: "The feathered arrow the gods of heaven gave Ame-no-Wakahiko. When he shot heaven's messenger with it, the arrow came back and killed him.",
    story: `In the Kojiki, the gods of heaven send Ame-no-Wakahiko down to rule the land on earth, giving him the heavenly bow Ame-no-Makakoyumi and the feathered arrows Ame-no-Habaya. But he marries a daughter of Ōkuninushi, the god of the land, and sends no word for eight years.

When the gods of heaven sent the pheasant Nakime to ask why, Ame-no-Wakahiko shot the pheasant dead with this arrow. The arrow pierced the pheasant's breast, flew up to heaven and fell before the god Takamimusuhi.

Takamimusuhi saw blood on the arrow and, declaring that if Ame-no-Wakahiko had evil intent he would be struck by it, hurled the arrow back down. The arrow struck Ame-no-Wakahiko in the chest as he lay asleep in the morning. The word kaeshi-ya, 'the returning arrow,' is said to come from this.`,
